[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jtidy/jtidy/issues/comments/1692192448","html_url":"https://github.com/jtidy/jtidy/issues/63#issuecomment-1692192448","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jtidy/jtidy/issues/63","id":1692192448,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBtgMtM5k3M7A","user":{"login":"kadampriyanka1109","id":31645495,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNjQ1NDk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31645495?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kadampriyanka1109","html_url":"https://github.com/kadampriyanka1109","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kadampriyanka1109/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kadampriyanka1109/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kadampriyanka1109/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kadampriyanka1109/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kadampriyanka1109/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kadampriyanka1109/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kadampriyanka1109/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kadampriyanka1109/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kadampriyanka1109/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-24T18:14:53Z","updated_at":"2023-08-24T18:14:53Z","body":"@haumacher Can you please update on this?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jtidy/jtidy/issues/comments/1692192448/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jtidy/jtidy/issues/comments/1693710427","html_url":"https://github.com/jtidy/jtidy/issues/63#issuecomment-1693710427","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jtidy/jtidy/issues/63","id":1693710427,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBtgMtM5k8_hb","user":{"login":"haumacher","id":5607145,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MDcxNDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5607145?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher","html_url":"https://github.com/haumacher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-25T17:33:25Z","updated_at":"2023-08-25T17:33:25Z","body":"I can reproduce your problem.\r\n\r\nThe problem with these dependency checkers is that they do not check whether there is a vulnerability or not. Instead they check, whether the version number of your dependencies somehow matches some funny pattern somehow derived from the vulnerability report. \r\n\r\nThe [report in question](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-34623) says the following:\r\n\r\n![grafik](https://github.com/jtidy/jtidy/assets/5607145/73077144-b6c8-47c9-92d7-bdef651c2c24)\r\n\r\nThe \"version number\" mentioned here could be interpreted as \"Version 938\", which is higher than \"Version 1.0.4\". The additional problem with these vulnerability reports is that they do not reference the affected library with some canonical identifier - such as the maven coordinates. Therefore, the dependency checkers have no chance to correctly match the report to your dependencies in some situations. \r\n\r\nTo work around these inaccuracies, the checkers are frequently updated with additional exclude rules for false positive matches. Therefore, you have two options: Either simply add an exclude rule for this CVE to your checker plugin configuration after you updated to jtidy-1.0.4, or you can report the problem to the dependency checker project (https://github.com/jeremylong/DependencyCheck) and ask them to fix this false positive. \r\n\r\nReleasing a new version of jtidy will not help here  except I would choose the version number 939.0.0 what I'm not willing to do.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jtidy/jtidy/issues/comments/1693710427/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jtidy/jtidy/issues/comments/1693715993","html_url":"https://github.com/jtidy/jtidy/issues/63#issuecomment-1693715993","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jtidy/jtidy/issues/63","id":1693715993,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBtgMtM5k9A4Z","user":{"login":"haumacher","id":5607145,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MDcxNDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5607145?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher","html_url":"https://github.com/haumacher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/haumacher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-25T17:37:50Z","updated_at":"2023-08-25T17:37:50Z","body":"Added project reproducing the invalid vulnerability report - maybe you can use this if you decide reporting the false positive to the checker project.\r\n\r\n[jtidy-dependency.zip](https://github.com/jtidy/jtidy/files/12442271/jtidy-dependency.zip)\r\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jtidy/jtidy/issues/comments/1693715993/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]